# Regression rules: one rule per implemented opcode (plus known-combo rules).
# Used by tests/test_validation_oracle.py for deterministic testing.
# One rule per line; lines starting with # are comments.

# Zero-arg opcodes
:
c
u
l
d
r
t
[
]
{
}
f
k
K
q
C
E

# One-arg opcodes
$1
$!
^x
^0
p2
D3
D0
T3
T0
y3
Y3
z3
Z3
@s
@a
!z
>A
>5
<3
<9
'5
'0
+3
-3
.3
,3
%p
%a
R3
L3

# Two-arg opcodes
i2!
i0x
ss$
sap
o3x
o0y
x33
x05
*01
*23

# Three-arg opcodes (X: insert from memory — always rejects without memory op)
# XNM — these typically reject since no M opcode precedes them

# Memory and filter opcodes
M
=0p
=3a
B0A

# Known-broken combos (multi-opcode rules)
c$1$2
u]r
l^x$1
d[r
tss!
c i2! ss$
